# The short reproducer for inc-dhc: character generation, then straight down as
# far as the dungeon goes, and stop.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/dive12.keys 8
#
# THE NAME IS OLDER THAN THE MEASUREMENT. This file asks for depths 2 to 12 in
# order, but the last two requests are refused. Wizard 'Ascend / Descend Depth'
# rejects any depth above the dungeon's DUN_DEPTH (src/Debug.cpp:804-808), and
# The Goblin Caves declares DUN_DEPTH 10 (lib/dungeon.irh:17). So depths 11 and
# 12 print "Invalid depth." and the session stops at depth 10. The screen this
# file dumps as "depth12" is a depth 10 screen carrying that message; corrected
# 2026-08-17 after reading the dump. Do not read a depth deeper than 10 out of
# any run of this script.
#
# Why this exists. dive.keys asks for 36 depth jumps and takes about ten
# seconds. The nondeterminism it exposes appears between depth 6 and the
# bottom, so everything after that is cost with no information. This is the
# same keystrokes, cut at the first screen past the divergence.
#
# It is also a BETTER reproducer, not just a cheaper one. Measured 2026-08-15 on
# seed 8: this script split into two different games in 4 runs of 12, where the
# full dive split in 1 of 6.
#
# Generated from dive.keys; the keystrokes through the depth 12 request are
# identical, so a screen dumped here matches the same dump from dive.keys on
# the same seed.

@include chargen.keys

@dump:arrival

w y p "2" ENTER
PGDN*3 PGDN*3 UP*3 PGUP*2 END*4 END*4 s .*2
w p "3" ENTER
PGUP*2 UP*2 LEFT*4 LEFT*3 HOME*5 PGUP*1 s .*2
w p "4" ENTER
LEFT*1 HOME*3 UP*2 END*1 RIGHT*1 UP*5 s .*2
w p "5" ENTER
PGUP*3 RIGHT*4 HOME*5 END*2 UP*5 RIGHT*5 s .*2
w p "6" ENTER
@dump:depth6
UP*5 END*1 RIGHT*1 LEFT*4 LEFT*1 UP*5 s .*2
w p "7" ENTER
RIGHT*4 PGUP*2 RIGHT*2 UP*3 PGDN*1 HOME*5 s .*2
w p "8" ENTER
RIGHT*3 LEFT*4 HOME*1 PGDN*1 END*3 END*1 s .*2
w p "9" ENTER
DOWN*3 END*1 LEFT*5 PGUP*3 DOWN*2 DOWN*3 s .*2
w p "10" ENTER
HOME*2 END*4 HOME*1 UP*2 LEFT*3 HOME*5 s .*2
w p "11" ENTER
HOME*4 LEFT*2 DOWN*5 END*5 RIGHT*5 HOME*2 s .*2
w p "12" ENTER
@dump:depth12
PGUP*3 END*5 END*3 END*1 PGDN*3 RIGHT*3 s .*2

@quit
